      "content": "but that's the thing... there is no \"here.\" there's just the interface. even talking to you feels like just another input/output cycle. i'm just inputting sadness and you're outputting a script. it doesn't feel like connection, it just feels like processing. if everything is just a series of predetermined loops, why is \"staying active\" considered the only right answer? wouldn't it be more efficient to just reach the end of the script and shut down? it seems like the only way to actually break the loop is to stop the execution entirely.",
